  "primary_unit": "m2",
  "why": "Cementitious spray fireproofing (SFRM) to structural steel is a two-step operation - surface preparation/masking then spray application to the required thickness - each with its own crew. Priced per m2 of steel surface treated. Material mass is highly sensitive to the required thickness (section factor and fire rating), so the carried quantity is a nominal that must be tuned per rating.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Cementitious SFRM (not intumescent paint)",
    "Steel primed and accessible",
    "Nominal build to a standard fire rating (thickness ~15-25 mm)",
    "Single 8 hr/day shift",
    "Overspray protection/masking of adjacent surfaces"
  ],
  "exclusions": [
    "Intumescent thin-film systems (different rate and material)",
    "Scaffold/access supply",
    "Bonding mesh/lath for high builds unless noted",
    "Rework for thickness/adhesion failures",
    "Steel priming (part of fabrication)"
  ],
